git log --oneline|head -3; git diff 9365073 HEAD | grep '^[+-]' | cut -c1-1800"]], "output": "```console\nefbe252 Brief: precise gain at k=5\n4ac86e3 Brief rev. 7: interim results, T1 as decomposition, rank claim dropped, margin and protocol decisions\n9365073 Brief rev. 6: align with pre-registration\n--- a/Brief.md\n+++ b/Brief.md\n-# Brief — the idea (rev. 6: aligned with the experiment-repo pre-registration)\n+# Brief — the idea (rev. 7: after the interim results; contribution (ii) reworded)\n-The machinery is classical: item selection by A-/D-optimal design for a latent trait vector (multidimensional computerized adaptive testing, Mulder & van der Linden 2009), cold-start active learning for matrix factorisation (Rashid 2002, Golbandi 2011, Houlsby 2014), probabilistic PCA, greedy subset selection with submodularity-ratio guarantees. **I do not claim a new selection method.** The contribution is: (i) the empirical answer on real leaderboard matrices under the protocol that matches the use (whole new models held out, by group; selection fit on others only); (ii) a sufficiency rule k*(ε) tied to the spectrum of the matrix, with its misfit term made explicit; (iii) the **scope map**: where the answer holds and where it never reaches the floor (extrapolation to new families/strongest models, sparse coverage, small M, saturated scores, task granularity), including a misspecification ladder on synthetic data on which real matrices are placed.\n+The machinery is classical: item selection by A-/D-optimal design for a latent trait vector (multidimensional computerized adaptive testing, Mulder & van der Linden 2009), cold-start active learning for matrix factorisation (Rashid 2002, Golbandi 2011, Houlsby 2014), probabilistic PCA, greedy subset selection with submodularity-ratio guarantees. **I do not claim a new selection method.** The contribution is: (i) the empirical answer on real leaderboard matrices under the protocol that matches the use (whole new models held out, by group; selection fit on others only); (ii) the **empirical needed-k curve** k*(ε) (excess over the all-others floor, with group-bootstrap CI), an **error decomposition** (residual floor + design term + misfit) that attributes where the error sits at each k, and a test of whether a spectrum-based rule predicts k* (interim result: it does not; see \"Interim results\" below; the failure and its cause are part of the contribution); (iii) the **scope map**: where the answer holds and where it never reaches the floor (extrapolation to new families/strongest models, sparse coverage, small M, saturated scores, task granularity), including a misspecification ladder on synthetic data on which real matrices are placed.\n-H1 matrices are close to low-rank (rank by the stated estimator). H2 designed selection beats random-k with the same inference for k below ~r and the gap closes afterwards. H3 measured curve follows T1/T2 on synthetic data (with estimation term) and on real data up to the reported misfit. H4 adaptivity gains only under misspecification. H5 conclusions weaken, quantifiably, under extrapolation, sparsity, small M, saturation, granularity.\n+H1 matrices are close to low-rank (rank by the stated estimator) — **interim: not supported as a rank claim** (estimators disagree: PA 5/8/10, CV 16, Gavish–Donoho 56; one component carries 63%); reworded to \"a dominant general factor plus a slowly decaying spectrum\", no \"rank r\" language. H2 designed selection beats random-k with the same inference for k below ~r and the gap closes afterwards. H3 measured curve follows T1/T2 on synthetic data (with estimation term) and on real data up to the reported misfit — **interim: the decomposition holds as an attribution, but the spectrum-based k\\*(ε) rule fails on real data** (predicted 3, measured 20 [12, 32] at ε = δ_floor ≈ 1.2 pt). H4 adaptivity gains only under misspecification. H5 conclusions weaken, quantifiably, under extrapolation, sparsity, small M, saturation, granularity.\n+\n+## Interim results and decisions (rev. 7; experiment-repo main G/T/S runs, scored on R_m \\ S, not \n[truncated for publication]", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "1d9d4612-6806-5ce9-8962-fcd2616c7308", "at": 1795731954.6432738, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27164, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "3ebaf229-1bff-5c91-8750-8f56b283143c", "at": 1795731954.64588, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27165, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "463a8563-2518-57c4-bc6d-fc785be9d0c8", "at": 1795731954.648794, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27166, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "ff74a8cc-926c-5d07-88a3-272c937e6a93", "at": 1795731954.716501, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27168, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "unknown", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "credential-required", "label": "challenge → credential-required", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cr