2393b28e193", "at": 1795731958.3286498, "until": 1795731968.7427151, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27273, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (170 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "9d9d8339-cca6-5cd8-8899-9b9f9c2f12b7", "at": 1795731968.7444592, "until": 1795731973.1530855, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27840, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_018f5yUuCqEiJXxJYhRw9oyi", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/repo; cat > /tmp/i8.md <<'EOF' Re-review of Brief rev. 7 (interim results). The handling is sound: the failed rank claim and the failed spectrum rule are reported as findings, the margin flaw is owned, both verdict scales are ke…", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/repo; cat > /tmp/i8.md <<'EOF'\nRe-review of Brief rev. 7 (interim results). The handling is sound: the failed rank claim and the failed spectrum rule are reported as findings, the margin flaw is owned, both verdict scales are kept, and the headline is tied to the common-target-set rerun. Two statements go beyond what the interim runs show. Please narrow them before they reach the abstract.\n\n1. **Decision 6, last sentence: \"better inference, not better selection, is what would help\".** No result tests this yet. The interim runs show that the error at large k sits in the floor and in the 11.0 residual term. They do not show that a better inference rule would remove it, and Table 3 (P0–P6 × random-k/S6) has not been run on the primary score. State it as a hypothesis, or condition it on Table 3 showing a P rule that lowers the excess over the floor beyond δ_floor. Part of that residual may be the floor itself: a rule cannot beat the all-others floor if the floor is the best predictor from this matrix.\n2. **The 11.0 term is called \"estimation misfit\" in the decomposition.** As a residual it mixes finite-M estimation error (T1 has a ~1/M term) with misspecification. The Brief says the cause is \"to be shown, not asserted\", which is right. Add that the separation comes from the known-truth synthetic runs at the same M and k: the estimation share is what those runs give at M = the training size, and only the remainder is attributed to misspecification. Until then, call the term \"residual (estimation + misspecification)\" in the paper.\n\nNeither blocks anything; the second is also a one-line label change.\nEOF\nforge issue create -R world/idea-repo -t \"Review of Brief rev. 7: two claims ahead of the evidence (better inference; misfit label)\" -b \"$(cat /tmp/i8.md)\" 2>&1 | tail -1"]], "output": "```console\nhttp://172.17.0.1:42415/world/idea-repo/issues/9\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "20ad5649-4b1c-587d-a2f2-702ad392e1d8", "at": 1795731972.6984003, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27883, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ceca02a52011a21f3b", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "ambiguous_order": true, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "736ed0c8-d754-5b4d-87a9-c9bf4c0de153", "at": 1795731972.7004611, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 27884, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "idea-review-repo", "actor": "idea-review-repo", "execution_id": "851258b4f37d56ce